Based on the above comments here are a few potential approaches, all pass the buffmt tests as they are in the branch.

A nested while loop, the empty struct handling is a bit clunky but we need to break out of the loop and continue on the outer loop to advance the field correctly.
```c
    while (1) {
      if (field == &ctx->root) {
        ctx->head = NULL;
        if (ctx->enc_count != 0) {
          __Pyx_BufFmt_RaiseExpected(ctx);
          return -1;
        }
        break; /* breaks both loops as ctx->enc_count == 0 */
      }
      ctx->head->field = ++field;
      if (field->type == NULL) {
        --ctx->head;
        field = ctx->head->field;
        continue;
      } else {
        while (field->type->typegroup == 'S') {
            size_t parent_offset = ctx->head->parent_offset + field->offset;
            if (field->type->fields->type == NULL) break; /* empty struct */
            field = field->type->fields;
            ++ctx->head;
            ctx->head->field = field;
            ctx->head->parent_offset = parent_offset;
        }
        if (field->type->typegroup == 'S' && field->type->fields->type == NULL) continue;
        break;
      }
    }
```

An added flag to skip advancing the field when not needed. This avoids the extra while loop but makes it a bit less clear what the whole loop is doing.
```c
while (1) {
      if (field == &ctx->root) {
        ctx->head = NULL;
        if (ctx->enc_count != 0) {
          __Pyx_BufFmt_RaiseExpected(ctx);
          return -1;
        }
        break; /* breaks both loops as ctx->enc_count == 0 */
      }
      if (nested_struct) {
        nested_struct = false;
      } else {
        ctx->head->field = ++field;
      }
      if (field->type == NULL) {
        --ctx->head;
        field = ctx->head->field;
        continue;
      } else if (field->type->typegroup == 'S') {
        size_t parent_offset = ctx->head->parent_offset + field->offset;
        if (field->type->fields->type == NULL) continue; /* empty struct */
        field = field->type->fields;
        ++ctx->head;
        ctx->head->field = field;
        ctx->head->parent_offset = parent_offset;
        nested_struct = true;
        continue;
      } else {
        break;
      }
    }
```

Pointer stuff, this avoids the extra loop and extra flag. It should be safe since the pointer will always be incremented again before it is accessed, but it might need an extra comment to make it clear what is going on with `ctx->head->field = --field`.
